<%# locals: (subject:, link_access:, truncate_length: 40, link_class: "text-cobalt-600 hover:text-cobalt-800", muted_class: "text-gray-500") %>
<%# The "Bezug" of a booked time: its ticket, its meeting, or nothing. One cell for
    all three billing views (aggregated / chronological / customer_export) so a
    fourth subject type is added in time_session_subject_presentation alone. Before
    this cell existed each view read .ticket directly and rendered meeting-booked
    time as "Ohne Ticket" — a billing line the customer could not account for.

    link_access is the (project_id, area) => bool map the controller precomputed
    (see #build_subject_link_access). Deliberately NOT asked per row: each answer
    costs a project_permissions query. Unknown key means "not allowed" — a cell
    rendered without its map shows titles without links rather than leaking one.

    Both types keep their glyph HERE, deliberately, while the time list shows a
    glyph only where there is no number (SubjectPresentation#glyph_as_handle?).
    The list has a column per part and a "#89" of its own to identify a ticket
    with; this cell has one line holding both types at once, where a glyph on
    only one of them reads as a flag rather than as a type. %>
<% if (parts = time_session_subject_presentation(subject)) %>
  <% label = truncate(parts.label, length: truncate_length) %>
  <% if link_access[[subject.project_id, parts.read_area]] %>
    <%= link_to parts.path, class: "#{link_class} inline-flex items-baseline gap-1.5 break-words", data: { turbo_frame: "_top" } do %>
      <i class="bi <%= parts.icon %>"></i><%= label %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <span class="<%= muted_class %> inline-flex items-baseline gap-1.5 break-words">
      <i class="bi <%= parts.icon %>"></i><%= label %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <span class="<%= muted_class %> italic"><%= t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.without_subject') %></span>
<% end %>
